<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enrico Dandolo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1107–<a href="/years/1205">1205</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enrico Dandolo was Doge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> from 1192, elected in old age and nearly blind. He led the Venetian part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, diverting it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zara</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, which the crusaders sacked in 1204. Venice gained a large share of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, the basis of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stato-da-mar">Stato da Mar</a>, and he died in Constantinople in 1205.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enrico-dandolo.jpg" alt="Enrico Dandolo" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grosso_of_Enrico_Dandolo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
